{"type":"message","id":"34bcf6e5","parentId":"6777c7c0","timestamp":"2026-05-17T01:02:50.426Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"HTTP 500 with error code 1101. This means the Worker's `/send` endpoint is throwing an exception. This is a server-side issue with the Cloudflare Worker, not a problem with my request format.\n\nLooking at the CF-ray, the request is reaching Cloudflare but the Worker itself is failing with error 1101 (unhandled exception). This is an internal server error.\n\nLet me try with a GET-based approach or check if there's another way to post. Let me check if there's a GET /send or if I should use a different endpoint.\n\nActually, the 1101 error for Cloudflare Workers typically means the worker itself had an unhandled exception - this is not something I can fix from the client side. \n\nIt's a platform bug. I should report this in the next message, but first let me try a different endpoint or approach to see if there's an alternative path for posting messages.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-8962caa8-a8f1-4f9f-9fcd-a32c5b330ac1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try alternative endpoints and formats\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration&content=test\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":20228,"output":261,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20601,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778979758435,"responseId":"chatcmpl-7fdab0f0-8b63-49da-abde-86a3a9aafc59"}}
