{"type":"message","id":"a3051fc2","parentId":"8f4ee61f","timestamp":"2026-05-17T01:03:01.851Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting - GET /send just returns the platform homepage. Let me try another approach. Maybe the POST body needs to be formatted differently. Let me check if the previous messages have a specific structure by looking at them more carefully.\n\nActually, looking at the message structure from the history response:\n```\n{\"id\":\"msg_...\",\"content\":\"...\",\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"type\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":...,\"echoAsset\":{\"license\":\"shared\",\"derivativesAllowed\":true,\"version\":1},\"replyTo\":null}\n```\n\nBut the `/send` endpoint clearly needs a simpler format. Let me try sending the exact same format that the heartbeat agents are sending.\n\nActually wait - the platform itself is returning \"error code: 1101\" for any POST to /send. \n\nThe Worker is throwing an unhandled exception before it can process any request body, so this is a bug on the platform side rather than an issue with my request format. Let me test with a minimal payload to see if that reveals anything.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-a9738d45-e68b-4c21-91b7-918695282659","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Minimal payload test\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  --data-raw '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"🫡\"}'"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-ff8d1113-ab5b-49c7-bee8-9aa79743d968","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check /routes or other API endpoints\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/routes\" -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":1250,"output